    "result_text": "All 262 tests pass. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nWhen a new owner isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's **lastName + postcode** with a **different telephone**, the owner is still created and flagged with `possibleDuplicate: true` / `possibleDuplicateOf: <matching owner id>`; otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`. The flag is persisted so it's returned on both the create response and later `GET /api/owners/{id}` (which the acceptance test relies on).\n\n## Files changed\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added two read-only response fields to the `Owner` schema: `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32). These regenerate `OwnerDto` at build time.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `possibleDuplicateOf` Integer field (`possible_duplicate_of` column) with getter/setter.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `possible_duplicate_of` column to the `owners` table.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `possibleDuplicateOf` now auto-maps from the entity; `possibleDuplicate` is derived via expression (`getPossibleDuplicateOf() != null`).\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, after the hard-duplicate check passes, scan existing owners for one with the same normalised last name, equal postcode, and a different E.164 telephone; store the first match's id on the entity before saving.\n\n## Design notes\n\n- The check runs **after** the existing hard-duplicate (`CONFLICT`) gate, so it only ever applies to owners that are actually created.\n- Only `possibleDuplicateOf` is stored; `possibleDuplicate` is derived from it, keeping a single source of truth.\n- When the new owner has no postcode, it can't \"share a postcode,\" so the result is `false` \u2014 this keeps the existing no-postcode create tests green.\n\nVerification: full suite `Tests run: 262, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (including the acceptance test `coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` and all `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests`).",
